%% class: center

# The rest of the language

Constructs the first showcase left out, plus the three plugin features that are easiest to miss.

---

%% toc

## On this deck

---

## Tabs

::: tabs
:::: tab [Symptom]
The upgrade runs, and half the finders are gone.

- No error, no exit code
- Only the tables with a behavior
::::

:::: tab [Cause]
|= What ran |= Against |
| The rule set | 4.5 sources |
| The finder rename | Nothing it matched |
::::

:::: tab [Fix]
1. Bump the dependency
2. Run the rules again
3. Re-run the touched tests

> The order is the fix.
::::
:::

{.note}
:::
`--extension tabs`. Any block goes in a tab: prose, a table, a list, a quote. Up
and down switch tabs, left and right stay with the deck.
:::

---

## Code groups

::: code-group
```bash [Composer]
composer require cakephp/cakephp:^5.2
```

```json [composer.json]
{ "require": { "cakephp/cakephp": "^5.2" } }
```

```php [Application.php]
$this->addPlugin('Migrations');
```
:::

{.note}
:::
`--extension codeGroup`. One block per file, switched on screen and unfolded in the PDF.
:::

---

## Details, folded away

::: details
### The long version of why buffering changed

5.0 always buffered result sets, which raised memory on large exports. 5.1 brought back `disableBufferedResults()`.
:::

{.note}
:::
Useful for the question you only sometimes get asked.
:::

---

## A table with block content

::: list-table
- - *Step*
  - *Command*
  - *Guards it*

- - Deprecations

  - ```bash
    bin/cake upgrade rector --rules cakephp45 src
    ```

  - Tests

- - The jump

  - ```bash
    composer update -W
    ```

  - Tests, PHPStan
:::

---

## Spoilers and swatches

The answer to "how long does the upgrade take" is :spoiler[as long as your test suite is short].

Palette: :color[#d33c43] accent, :color[#1f7a4d] success, :color[#6b7280] muted.

---

## Diffs and line numbers

{.diff}
```js
  let icon = document.querySelector('li.file-entry > span.icon');
- icon.classList.add('icon-file-text');
+ icon.classList.remove('icon-file-text');
```

{data-line-numbers}
```php
$table->updateQuery()
    ->set(['published' => true])
    ->execute();
```

{.note}
:::
`{.diff}` colours the changed lines, `{data-line-numbers}` numbers them. Both are plain Carve attribute lines.
:::

---

## Code with callouts

```php
$query = $this->Articles->selectQuery();   <1>
$query->contain(['Authors'])               <2>
    ->where(['published' => true]);
```

<1> One query type, so the IDE and PHPStan know what comes next.
<2> Eager loading, which is the whole point of the slide.

{.note}
:::
`--extension codeCallouts`. The markers bind to the list under the block.
:::

